Yes, I agree with you. This is the main problem with this patch. Actually,
when I started to think about the songs, I searched for pages about the
AD&D bard on the internet looking for inspiration, and got too much cool
ideas from it. Then when I saw this was going to turn out to be another
spellcasting system inside nethack (like the existing one, but requiring
instruments to 'cast'), I tried to think a way to avoid this. The solution
I found was to create some way to link songs and spells, so to each song
there is a corresponding spell, and songs mimic spells but with slightly
different effects. Players with music skill can song the spells using
different instruments (only bards could play songs which spells they don't
know yet).

Well, this is what the current patch does. But now it's almost complete,
and reading your comment, I feel I have created a monster; while it tries
not to create another spell system, it complicates things a lot, trying to
hook in the existing one. And while some of the ideas for the AD&D bard
sounds really cool, they simply don't fit with the idea of a musician
using his ability to influence monsters.

So, the best thing to do is to strip off the whole 'songcasting' system,
and create simple songs that do well with the idea of a musician
influencing monsters. I'll try your suggestions... How about these: 
- sleep
- confuse
- scare
- paralyse (while the music is playing)
- pacify (angry monsters)
- make alliance (taming)
- berserk pets (make them attack, even peacefuls)
- calm pets (they stop attacking, and do not attack peacefuls)
- haste pets (they speed up while the song is played)

What the AD&D bard 'shout' does? I'm googling for it but found nothing.

And, how about a song to make a pet use its monster ability? Like making a
dragon breath attack, a black naga spit acid, and so on.


